1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
firstkey — a rental copilot for Geneva
Built for the Convex All Gas Hackathon

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:08,000
The public listing feed — live, no login required

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:16,000
Filter by rooms, budget, surface, and neighborhood
All client-side, instant — reactive Convex queries

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Sign in with Clerk to set up a real search profile

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,500
Budget, rooms, and a personal pitch —
sent with every application

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Real matches. Firecrawl indexes these listings
straight from agency websites —

7
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:46,000
before they ever reach the big rental portals

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:53,000
OpenAI (gpt-4o-mini) drafts a personalized
application from the renter's profile

9
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:58,000
Editable — nothing sends without a human reviewing it first

10
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Sending goes through AgentMail —
a real email, only on explicit click

11
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:12,000
A reply — arriving live, synced back
by AgentMail's webhook in real time

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The full thread: the application sent,
and the agency's real reply

13
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Status updates everywhere, live —
the public feed reflects the reply too

14
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Every listing links back to its real source —
straight from the agency's own site, not a portal

15
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,600
firstkey — built with Convex, Firecrawl, OpenAI, and AgentMail
